# Redis server extracted for the benchmark head-to-head (binaries + runtime state, not source)
.redis/

# JFR recordings. Never commit these.
#
# `-XX:StartFlightRecording=settings=profile` records the JVM's initial environment variables, so every
# recording taken on a developer machine embeds whatever was exported in that shell. The recordings from
# the discarded end-to-end run carried a live OPENAI_API_KEY into eight files; GitHub's push protection
# caught it. The analysis a .jfr supports is worth less than the risk of shipping one.
*.jfr
